  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Reconcile the two lenses and the conformance pass into one set of findings.\n\n## The conformance verdicts\n\n{{.inputs.layer_verdicts}}\n\n## Lens A — correctness and the next maintainer\n\n{{.inputs.findings_a}}\n\n## Lens B — the person we serve, and the operator at 3am\n\n{{.inputs.findings_b}}\n\n## The deliverables\n\n{{.inputs.features}}\n\n## The changes\n\n{{.inputs.changes}}\n\n## How to merge\n\n**Dedupe** where the two lenses found the same defect, and mark it `lens: both`.\nTwo lenses independently reaching the same finding is the strongest signal in this\nwhole pass — do not let deduplication erase it.\n\n**Keep disagreements as separate rows.** Where one lens calls something a blocker\nand the other calls it a note, that is not a conflict to resolve by averaging. It\nis information: record both, attributed. The confidence score reads critic\ndisagreement as the cheapest real calibration available, and flattening it here\nthrows that away.\n\n**Attribute every finding** to a lens (`a`, `b`, `both`, or `conformance`) and to\na **deliverable id**. A finding that cannot name an id is a note.\n\n**Before recording a finding, write the strongest argument that it is not a\nproblem.** If that argument holds, it was a note. Carry the counterargument on the\nrow so the person reading the gate can see it was tried.\n\n## `failing_layer`\n\nThe **earliest** layer with a blocker. Earliest, because a UX blocker makes the UI\nfindings moot — sending the run back to UI would fix screens against a flow that\nis itself wrong.\n\nName it as the **phase the root re-enters**: `product`, `ux`, `ui`,\n`engineering`, `implementation`, `acceptance`, or `documentation`. A failing\n*Standards* row is not a phase — attribute it to the phase that made the silent\ndeparture.\n\nLeave it absent when there is no blocker.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nEverything that is real but not blocking, plus **every deferred deletion from\nphase 5** and **every unbuilt deliverable with `importance >= 0.5`**. Those two\nare the ones that quietly never happen.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`findings` — severity (`blocker` · `should-fix` · `note`), claim, evidence\n(`path:line` or a reproduction), deliverable_id, lens, and the strongest\ncounterargument.\n\n`failing_layer` — the phase, or absent.\n\n`follow_ups` — as above.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "findings": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "required": [
                "severity",
                "claim",
                "lens"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "severity": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "blocker",
                    "should-fix",
                    "note"
                  ]
                },
                "claim": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "evidence": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "path:line, or a reproduction."
                },
                "deliverable_id": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "lens": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "a",
                    "b",
                    "both",
                    "conformance"
                  ]
                },
                "strongest_counterargument": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "description": "Recorded before the finding is. If it holds, this was a note."
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "failing_layer": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": [
              "product",
              "ux",
              "ui",
              "engineering",
              "implementation",
              "acceptance",
              "documentation"
            ]
          },
          "follow_ups": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "findings",
          "follow_ups"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "slotMeta": {
    "outputs.failing_layer": {
      "optional": true
    }
  }
}
